cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Curated Formula 1 Telemetry and Race Session Dataset (2024 full season)"
message: "If you use this dataset or the curation code, please cite both this work and the underlying F1 timing data source."
type: dataset
authors:
  - family-names: Marepalli
    given-names: Anand
    affiliation: "School of Information Sciences, University of Illinois Urbana-Champaign"
    email: anandm5@illinois.edu
abstract: >
  An analysis-ready, lifecycle-curated dataset derived from public Formula 1
  session data accessed through the FastF1 Python library and Jolpica-F1.
  Three layers (bronze NDJSON, silver and gold dbt-managed tables in a
  single-file DuckDB warehouse, exported to Parquet+CSV for the deposit)
  are produced via a Kafka + dbt + Airflow pipeline. Covers the full 2024
  F1 season (24 rounds, 120 sessions). Includes lap timing, sector splits,
  tire compounds, pit stop indicators, race results, driver and team
  metadata, and weather snapshots. Documentation includes a Dublin Core
  metadata record, data dictionary, cleaning log, provenance log
  (PROV-O JSON-LD), and a Zenodo-ready preservation bundle. Curated as
  the IS547 (Spring 2026) self-directed course project.
keywords:
  - "Formula 1"
  - "motorsport"
  - "telemetry"
  - "data curation"
  - "medallion architecture"
  - "FAIR"
  - "reproducible research"
  - "dbt"
  - "DuckDB"
  - "Apache Kafka"
license: "CC-BY-4.0"
